    "title_key": "bayernmunichsmichaelolisesettomisslillegame",
    "body": "Bayern Munich face Lille in the UEFA Champions League on Wednesday night, but they will likely be without Michael Olise after the Frenchman suffered an injury in Friday’s 1-1 draw against Cologne . Olise left the Allianz Arena on crutches after a challenge from Tom Krauß at the edge of the box, resulting in the player’s substitution during the half-time break. The good news, though, is that the 24-year-old didn’t suffer a serious injury, only bruising to his left foot. As reported by BILD , Olise is wearing a VACOped brace to help with the recovery process, but Bayern president Herbert Hainer doesn’t believe the attacker will be fit for Wednesday’s game in France. “He won’t be gone for long, but the Champions League game is probably out of the question: maybe [he will return] in Hamburg,” he explained. Olise has scored 12 goals and provided seven assists in 16 matches across all competitions for Vincent Kompany’s Bayern this season. GGFN | Daniel Pinder",
